From b96b0f194eda3dcdc544aa778601b65fad5ad653 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Lepikhov <andrei.lepikhov@pgedge.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:38:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix log_min_messages comparison in emit-log hook for
 PostgreSQL 19

PostgreSQL 19 changed the log_min_messages GUC from a plain int into
an int array indexed by backend type (see is_log_level_output() and
its callers in src/backend/utils/error/elog.c). In the emit-log hook
filter that replaced the pg18-020-LOG-to-DEBUG1 core patch, the
comparison 'log_min_messages < edata->elevel' therefore compares the
array pointer against the error level on PG19 and later, which
compiles with only a warning and yields an arbitrary result, so the
demoted DEBUG1 message may be exposed to (or hidden from) the server
log regardless of the actual setting.

Use log_min_messages[MyBackendType] under PG_VERSION_NUM >= 190000,
matching what core's is_log_level_output() callers do; miscadmin.h is
already included. Same fix as already applied on the pg19-v5_STABLE
port branch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/spock.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/spock.c b/src/spock.c
index 0d23c2f..4b215d1 100644
--- a/src/spock.c
+++ b/src/spock.c
@@ -989,7 +989,11 @@ log_message_filter(ErrorData *edata)
 		if (lower_output_level)
 		{
 			/* Reconsider decision on exposing the message */
+#if PG_VERSION_NUM >= 190000
+			if (log_min_messages[MyBackendType] < edata->elevel)
+#else
 			if (log_min_messages < edata->elevel)
+#endif
 				edata->output_to_server = false;
 			if (client_min_messages < edata->elevel)
 				edata->output_to_client = false;
